{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To find the minimum value of the function \\( f(x) = \\sqrt{-x^2 + 4x + 21} - \\sqrt{-x^2 + 3x + 10} \\), we first need to determine the domain of the function. The expressions under the square roots must be non-negative.\n\nFor the first square root, we have:\n\\[\n-x^2 + 4x + 21 \\geq 0 \\implies x^2 - 4x - 21 \\leq 0.\n\\]\nThe roots of the quadratic equation \\( x^2 - 4x - 21 = 0 \\) are \\( x = -3 \\) and \\( x = 7 \\). Therefore, the inequality \\( x^2 - 4x - 21 \\leq 0 \\) holds for \\( -3 \\leq x \\leq 7 \\).\n\nFor the second square root, we have:\n\\[\n-x^2 + 3x + 10 \\geq 0 \\implies x^2 - 3x - 10 \\leq 0.\n\\]\nThe roots of the quadratic equation \\( x^2 - 3x - 10 = 0 \\) are \\( x = -2 \\) and \\( x = 5 \\). Therefore, the inequality \\( x^2 - 3x - 10 \\leq 0 \\) holds for \\( -2 \\leq x \\leq 5 \\).\n\nThe domain of \\( f(x) \\) is the intersection of the two intervals, which is \\( -2 \\leq x \\leq 5 \\).\n\n","prefix_end":875,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":true,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,1477,279,8028,897,315,279,729,17767,282,2075,8,284,1124,26888,19999,87,61,17,488,220,19,87,488,220,17,16,92,481,1124,26888,19999,87,61,17,488,220,18,87,488,220,16,15,92,1124,701,582,1156,1184,311,8253,279,7947,315,279,729,13,576,23393,1212,279,9334,19703,1969,387,2477,60935,382,2461,279,1156,9334,3704,11,582,614,510,59,9640,6558,61,17,488,220,19,87,488,220,17,16,1124,709,80,220,15,1124,6383,550,856,61,17,481,220,19,87,481,220,17,16,1124,273,80,220,15,624,59,921,785,19703,315,279,79151,23606,17767,856,61,17,481,220,19,87,481,220,17,16,284,220,15,1124,8,525,17767,856,284,481,18,1124,8,323,17767,856,284,220,22,1124,568,15277,11,279,31205,17767,856,61,17,481,220,19,87,481,220,17,16,1124,273,80,220,15,1124,8,9982,369,17767,481,18,1124,273,80,856,1124,273,80,220,22,1124,3593,2461,279,2086,9334,3704,11,582,614,510,59,9640,6558,61,17,488,220,18